  <description>
    <p>Outputs 1 when the input lies within [LowerLimit, UpperLimit], else 0.</p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Module</td><td><code>nflow_blocks</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library</td><td>Logic / Bit Operations</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>intervalTest</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Label</td><td>Interval Test</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><img src="../../../../libraries/logic/exports/intervalTest.svg" align="middle"/></p>
    <p><b>Description</b></p>
    <p>Tests whether the input <code>u</code> lies inside a static interval. The bounds <code>LowerLimit</code> and <code>UpperLimit</code> are parameters; <code>IntervalClosedLeft</code> and <code>IntervalClosedRight</code> select whether each end is inclusive (<code>&gt;=</code>/<code>&lt;=</code>) or exclusive (<code>&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;</code>). The test is applied element-wise over a vector input.</p>
    <p>Pure algebraic feedthrough (no state): the output at each step depends only on the current input.</p>
    <p><b>Ports</b></p>
    <p><b>Input(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Numeric signal read by the block.</td><td>left</td><td>x=0, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Output(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Numeric signal produced by the block.</td><td>right</td><td>x=100, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Parameters</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>LowerLimit</code></td><td>0</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>UpperLimit</code></td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IntervalClosedLeft</code></td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IntervalClosedRight</code></td><td>1</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Block Characteristics</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Block type</td><td>intervalTest</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Family</td><td>Logic / Bit Operations</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rendered size</td><td>100 x 80</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phases</td><td>ALGEBRAIC</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Internal state or history</td><td>no</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Signal data type</td><td>double numeric values</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Algorithms</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>ALGEBRAIC: out = (u &gt;= LowerLimit) &amp;&amp; (u &lt;= UpperLimit) ? 1 : 0, with strict comparisons when the corresponding end is open.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Equation or Rule</b></p>
    <latex>y = \begin{cases} 1 &amp; \text{lo} \le u \le \text{up} \\ 0 &amp; \text{otherwise} \end{cases}</latex>
    <p><b>Extended Capabilities</b></p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
